{
  "description": "Scenario tests for the WEST-A CQL logic. Each case starts from vital signs that all score 0 (respiration rate 16, oxygen saturation 97, room air, systolic 120, pulse 70, alert, temperature 37.0) and changes the values in vitals; null leaves a parameter unmeasured. extra adds observations, with minutesEarlier (negative for later), status, unit (instead of the profile's unit) and period (timed with effectivePeriod). parameters are passed to both libraries; a parameter not given is passed as null, except the Booleans, which are false. Priority codes: 1 Röd, 2 Orange, 3 Gul, 4 Grön; a complaint priority with a system is given as system|code. Triage Criteria is a list of codes from the WEST-A triage criterion code system (163 is no warning symptoms, 159-162 are the needs), each optionally given as system|code.",
